# Every Dockerfile copies the whole repo (the Maven reactor needs all modules present), so keep
# build-context junk out: it bloats the context, it can leak a stale host-built JAR into the image,
# and anything in here that changes often needlessly invalidates the `COPY . .` layer - and with it
# the Maven build - for all 14 images.
#
# `**/target/` rather than `target/` + `*/target/`: the old pair only reached one directory deep.
**/target/
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
*.iml
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# Not inputs to the build. Editing a doc, the compose file, a Dockerfile or a helper script must
# not trigger a recompile of every service.
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
**/Dockerfile
**/README.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
scripts/

**/*.log
.DS_Store

